y5-compositor (1.4.1-1ubuntu2) resolute; urgency=medium

  First-time setup is no longer required: on first session start a
  complete default ~/.config/y5.compositor/settings.json is seeded
  automatically (an existing file is never touched). Customize any
  time with:

    y5.compositor.settings

  (package y5-compositor-settings; now a hard dependency of
  y5-compositor).

 -- Kacper Paczos <kacperpaczos2024@protonmail.com>  Fri, 17 Jul 2026 16:30:00 +0200

y5-compositor (1.4.1-1ubuntu1) resolute; urgency=medium

  The former monolithic y5-compositor package is split into components.
  `y5-compositor` is now the core session only.

  To keep the previous full bundle after upgrade:

    sudo apt install y5-compositor-full

  First-time setup still requires:

    y5.compositor.settings

  (package y5-compositor-settings; recommended by y5-compositor).

 -- Kacper Paczos <kacperpaczos2024@proton.me>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 18:15:00 +0200

y5-compositor (1.4.0-1ubuntu2) resolute; urgency=medium

  First-time setup: run `y5.compositor.settings` to create
  ~/.config/y5.compositor/settings.json, then log out and select the
  "Y5 Compositor" session from your display manager.

  Optional MX Master support:
    systemctl --user enable --now mx-gesture-daemon.service

 -- Kacper Paczos <kacperpaczos2024@proton.me>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 16:30:00 +0200
